1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,100
So many people are starting jiu-jitsu at an older age, more now than ever before.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:07,100
40's, 50's, even 60's, starting jiu-jitsu.

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:11,000
My father, for example, started at 64 years old, he's now 66 years old.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,900
When you start older, you're not the athlete that you were when you were in your 20's and 30's.

5
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,000
You're not as flexible, you may not even be as strong, agile,

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,600
and it may even be harder to learn things.

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,600
Your brain might be just burnt out from just life and learning things.

8
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,300
So when my father told me he wanted to start training jiu-jitsu, he really wanted to get his blue belt.

9
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,900
So I understand the techniques that you need to learn to get your blue belt.

10
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:33,600
A lot of those techniques he wasn't able to do because of his lack of flexibility and just move overall movement.

11
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,900
He's been a carpenter for 40 years and his body's just kind of taken its toll.

12
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:41,400
So I was teaching him jiu-jitsu privately and he was taking classes, he was doing that each week.

13
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:46,900
So there was a lot of limitations, so I had to decide how to teach him and I had to relearn how to teach someone jiu-jitsu.

14
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,500
So I started extremely basic.

15
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,800
From this position, you need to be thinking this, this, and this.

16
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,900
And I kind of mapped out what is the jiu-jitsu jump-start blueprint.

17
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,700
So the jump-start blueprint helped him with what to do from every single position.

18
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,500
Knowing what to do when you're on the mount.

19
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,500
Knowing what the person on bottom of you is trying to think about doing.

20
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,500
And once you have that knowledge of every position, what you should be thinking and what they should be thinking,

21
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:07,900
jiu-jitsu becomes pretty easy.

22
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,400
Now you could take the techniques that you're learning in the intro curriculum

23
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,300
and you could actually apply them based on the strategies from each position.

24
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:16,200
It jump-started his learning and helped him get way better, way faster

25
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:20,200
and he's actually slated to get his blue belt this December, assuming everything goes to plan.

26
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:23,500
So if you're starting jiu-jitsu at a later age, 40s, 50s, 60s,

27
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,300
jiu-jitsu still is for you, you just have to do it the right way.

28
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,700
You have to be careful of who you're training with and you have to have more knowledge,

29
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:33,300
more strategies to combat the fact that your body isn't what it used to be

30
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,000
and your athleticism isn't what it used to be.

31
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,700
And I teach you the exact way on how to do that in the jiu-jitsu jump-start blueprint.

32
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:42,900
So click the link below or comment jump-start and you'll time-collapse your learning curve

33
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:45,600
and learn the strategies to help you combat those young bucks.

